ng experimental, if there is a stability issue there?","created_at":"2023-11-21T09:56:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18434#issuecomment-1820584892","id":1820584892,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18434","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5sg-u8","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1820584892/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-21T09:56:52Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1820584892","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7277892?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Laurence-Cullen","id":7277892,"login":"Laurence-Cullen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzc4OTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14262417?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yashk2810","id":14262417,"login":"yashk2810","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjYyNDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14262417?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yashk2810","id":14262417,"login":"yashk2810","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjYyNDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\n\nWe are trying to implement `PositionalSharding` in a minimal case where we are are shifting values in an array and assigning new ones. We have observed that when jiting this `assign` function the outputs are different and incorrect when `array` has a `(8,1)` or `(2, 4)` shard topology. The sharding does not effect the unjited function.\r\n\r\nFrom inspection of the jited outputs on the topologies that fail, we have noticed the values from the right hand side of the initial  array end up at index `7` i.e. `jitted_assign(array, value)[7] == array[-1]`. The correct behaviour is `assign(array, value)[7] == array[8]`.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport os\r\n\r\n# Make 8 CPU devices\r\nos.environ[\"XLA_FLAGS\"] = '--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=8'\r\n\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\nimport jax.random\r\nfrom jax.experimental import mesh_utils\r\nfrom jax.sharding import PositionalSharding\r\n\r\n\r\ndef assign(array, value):\r\n    \"\"\"Shift the array to the left by one and set the rightmost column to value.\"\"\"\r\n    shifted = array.at[:-1, :].set(array[1:, :])\r\n    return shifted.at[-1, :].set(jnp.ones(array.shape[1]) * value)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    value = 1.456\r\n    N = 16\r\n    array = jax.random.uniform(jax.random.PRNGKey(1241), (N, N))\r\n\r\n    devices = mesh_utils.create_device_mesh((8,))\r\n    sharding = PositionalSharding(devices)\r\n\r\n    jitted_assign = jax.jit(assign)\r\n\r\n    # This works\r\n    array = jax.device_put(array, sharding.reshape(1, 8))\r\n    assert jnp.allclose(assign(array, value), jitted_assign(array, value))\r\n\r\n    # Correctly shifted output\r\n    assert jnp.allclose(assign(array, value)[7], array[8])\r\n\r\n    array = jax.device_put(array, sharding.reshape(8, 1))\r\n\r\n    # This should not pass\r\n    assert jnp.allclose(jitted_assign(array, value)[7], array[-1])\r\n\r\n    # This fails\r\n    assert jnp.allclose(assign(array, value), jitted_assign(array, value))\r\n\r\n    # This fails\r\n    array = jax.device_put(array, sharding.reshape(2, 4))\r\n    assert jnp.allclose(assign(array, value), jitted_assign(array, value))\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == '__main__':\r\n    main()\r\n```\r\n\r\nAny help to explain what is going on would be very appreciated, whether this is a bug or me just not understanding how sharding is expected to work.\n\n### What jax/jaxlib version are you using?\n\njax==0.4.16 jaxlib==0.4.16\n\n### Which accelerator(s) are you using?\n\nCPU\n\n### Additional system info\n\nPython 3.11.5, Ubuntu 22.04.3 LTS\n\n### NVIDIA GPU info\n\n_No response_","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":3,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18434/comments","created_at":"2023-11-08T14:54:52Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18434/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18434","id":1983795410,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":1104782284,"name":"bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTA0NzgyMjg0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/labels/bug"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18434/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOCTkjjc52PlDS","number":18434,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18434/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax","state":"open","state_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"completed":0,"percent_completed":0,"total":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18434/timeline","title":"Inconsistent behaviour of jited and non jited array assignment function on some `PositionalSharding` topologies.","type":null,"updated_at":"2023-11-21T10:02:03Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18434","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7277892?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence-Cullen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Laurence